# Analysis

The issue is in **markdownParser.js**: when parsing the Python file with a mermaid diagram (`mermaid` language fence), the parser treats the closing ` ``` ` of the mermaid block as a **closing fence for code**, not as content within a markdown block. This splits the file into multiple blocks instead of keeping it as one.

**Root cause**: The mermaid fence has `info="mermaid"`, so it's treated as opening a code block. When the closing ` ``` ` (with no info) is found, the parser closes it, treating everything after as new content.

**Solution**: Modify `parseBlocks()` to keep the mermaid diagram (and any content after it) as part of the same markdown/text block when inside a markdown context.

