if (inCodeBlock && isMarkdownBlockType(currentType) && fence) {
  currentContent.push(line)
  continue
}
```

**The bug:** This guard only protects markdown blocks! When `currentType = 'py'` (or any non-markdown type), the parser falls through to the fence handling logic below, which then opens a **new** block for the `mermaid` fence.

Then when the closing ` ``` ` of the mermaid block appears, `isClosingFence` matches it against the **mermaid fence** (length 3, char `` ` ``), closes that block — and the outer `py` block never gets properly closed.

