```

## Key changes

The old logic:
```js
// Only protected markdown blocks from inner fences
if (inCodeBlock && isMarkdownBlockType(currentType) && fence) {
  currentContent.push(line)
  continue
}
```

The new logic — unified handling for **all** block types:
```js
// All inner fences are content; only the matching closing fence ends the block
if (inCodeBlock && fence) {
  if (isClosingFence(line, currentFence)) {
    addBlock(true)
    inCodeBlock = false
  } else {
    currentContent.push(line)
  }
  continue
}
```

This also removes the now-dead anonymous fence / `allNestedClosed` code paths that were unreachable after the early `continue`, simplifying the overall flow significantly.

